# agent-hub configuration.
#
# install.sh copies this to /etc/agent-hub.env (mode 0600) if that file does not
# already exist, then you fill it in and `systemctl restart agent-hub`.
#
# Only two lines usually need changing: the Telegram token and the allowlist.

# --- Telegram (the recommended control surface) ------------------------------
# Create a bot: message @BotFather on Telegram, /newbot, and paste the token it
# gives you here. Long polling is outbound-only — no public hostname, no port
# forward, no tunnel needed.
AGENT_HUB_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=

# Numeric Telegram user ids allowed to run commands, comma separated.
# To find yours: start the service, message your bot /whoami, and it will tell
# you your id even before you are on the list.
#
# Every id here gets unsupervised shell access on this box through the sessions
# it can start, and can point the box at a Claude account. Treat it as a root
# allowlist, because that is what it is.
AGENT_HUB_TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=

# --- Web UI ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The HTTP server always runs (the SessionStart hook posts to it). It binds
# loopback by default, which needs no token because reaching it already implies
# shell access on the box.
#
# To publish the UI, keep this on 127.0.0.1 and put a Cloudflare Tunnel in front
# of it — the port then never listens on a routable interface:
#
#   cloudflared tunnel create agent-hub
#   cloudflared tunnel route dns agent-hub hub.example.com
#   # ingress: hostname hub.example.com -> service http://127.0.0.1:8790
#
# Set a token whenever the UI is reachable by anyone but you, tunnel or not.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 24
AGENT_HUB_BIND=127.0.0.1
AGENT_HUB_PORT=8790
AGENT_HUB_TOKEN=

# --- Sessions ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where sessions start. Must be a directory this user can write; agent-hub marks
# it trusted in ~/.claude.json so sessions never stop at the trust prompt.
#AGENT_HUB_WORKDIR=/root/agent-runs

# Concurrency cap. This counts EVERY live tmux session on the box, not just the
# ones agent-hub started. Raise it only if the box can genuinely take the load —
# the machine this pattern came from hard-froze at around 9 concurrent agents.
#AGENT_HUB_MAX_SESSIONS=5

# Bypass all permission prompts inside sessions (--dangerously-skip-permissions).
# On by default: an unattended session that stops for a prompt is a hung session.
# Override per session without changing this: /new <name> --safe keeps prompts
# on for that one session, /new <name> --dangerous bypasses them. The choice is
# recorded against the session, so resumes and boot restores keep it.
#AGENT_HUB_SKIP_PERMISSIONS=1

# Bring up Remote Control so sessions are drivable from claude.ai/code.
# Set to 0 if your account does not have Remote Control; sessions then have to be
# driven with `tmux attach`.
#AGENT_HUB_REMOTE_CONTROL=1

# Kill a session whose Remote Control never attached, instead of keeping it.
#AGENT_HUB_RC_REQUIRED=0

# Count and show tmux sessions agent-hub did not start. On by default so the cap
# reflects the box's real concurrency. Turn off on a shared box.
#AGENT_HUB_ADOPT_UNTRACKED=1

# --- Resume ------------------------------------------------------------------
# `claude --resume` on a large or stale conversation shows a blocking dialog
# first, asking whether to resume from a summary or in full. agent-hub answers
# it only when it is actually on screen.
#
#   ask      (default) show the dialog — age, token count, both options — and
#            hold the session there until someone chooses. Resuming a 350k-token
#            conversation in full is not a decision worth making blind.
#   summary  always take "Resume from summary (recommended)".
#   full     always resume the full session as-is.
# Naming a mode on the command (/resume <name> full) always wins.
#AGENT_HUB_RESUME_CHOICE=ask

# How long a session may sit waiting for that choice before taking the summary
# option by itself, so a forgotten /resume degrades safely instead of hanging.
#AGENT_HUB_RESUME_ASK_TIMEOUT_MS=600000

# Boot restore can never ask — nobody is present after a 3am reboot — so it
# always uses a concrete choice. summary (default) or full.
#AGENT_HUB_RESUME_CHOICE_UNATTENDED=summary

# Bring back sessions that were running when the box went down.
#AGENT_HUB_RESTORE_ON_START=1

# --- Claude account login ----------------------------------------------------
# Allow `/login` from chat and the web UI so a fresh box can be authenticated
# without SSH. Set to 0 to require SSH for authentication.
#AGENT_HUB_LOGIN=1

# --- Misc --------------------------------------------------------------------
#AGENT_HUB_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/agent-hub
#AGENT_HUB_CLAUDE_BIN=claude
#AGENT_HUB_LOG_LEVEL=info
